<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="31c7b786-4e6e-5787-9493-be3d06da552c" activityNameId="f6720647-c6e6-5bec-8c43-10b9f72f73b5" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Application, digested matter from biowaste in agricultural co-digestion, covered</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Application, digested matter from biowaste in agricultural co-digestion, covered
This process can only be used together with the process "biogas, mix, at agricultural co-fermentation, covered" because bio waste is not treated in agricultural biogas plants alone but only together with liquid manure. This process has been generated to give the possibility to model co-fermentation with different inputs. The multioutput-process "bio waste, to agriculture co-fermentation, covered" delivers the co-products "biogas",  "application of digested matter" and the service "disposal of bio waste". The functional unit refers to 1 kg fresh matter of vegetable and organic waste and catering waste. The allocation is based on economic criteria. ;
UUID: cbc085d1-8fa8-3ed4-8f71-19feb9c407c1
This process contains the infrastructure, the energy used and the emissions of the fermentation process.
Location: This dataset is valid for agricultural plants in Switzerland in the year 2006
Technology: To reduce methane emission the stock container is covered, to reduce NH3 emissions the digested matter will be spread with a trail hose.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 12 mio. m3 Biogas 
Sampling: field data, The data are the average of 20 plants in Switzerland to produce electricity according the criteria of "naturemade". 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cbc085d1-8fa8-3ed4-8f71-19feb9c407c1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
